\begin{frame}{Investment bank 2}
They do not make investments; they are not banks.  Revenue come from, 
\pause
\begin{itemize}[<+-| alert@+>]
\item Merger and acquisition, disposal of parts of business.  Business strategy. 
\item Raising capital: IPOs, bond issuance, syndicated loans. 
\item Making financial markets. 
\item "In the moving business not the storage business"
\end{itemize}
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}{Investment bank 3}
	Intermediation
\begin{itemize}[<+-| alert@+>]
		\pause
	\item Firms
		\begin{itemize}
			\item restructuring and advice and funding
		\end{itemize}
	\item Funds
		\begin{itemize}
			\item investments and advice and access
		\end{itemize}
	\item Government 
		\begin{itemize}
			\item advice about debt issuance
		\end{itemize}
\end{itemize}
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}{Funds 1}
There are a wide range of different types of fund
\pause
\begin{itemize}[<+-| alert@+>]
\item Pension funds
\item Insurance funds
\item Mutual funds or ETF
\item Hedge funds (Citadel Securities, Pod shops)
\item Private equity (SoftBank and Apollo)
\item Sovereign Wealth Funds
\end{itemize}
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}{Funds 2}
There is a distinction between 
\begin{itemize}[<+-| alert@+>]
\pause
\item The fund owners
\begin{itemize}
\item firm that runs the pension
\item insurance company
\item country, university or family
\end{itemize}
\item The fund managers
\begin{itemize}
\item BlackRock, Vanguard etc
\item specialist (asset or country) 
\end{itemize}
\end{itemize}
\end{frame}

